PASS C2 every branch with h2 != 0 is that central one (no non-central D enters [K,P]): so the ONLY way a scalar generator can appear in [K,P] is a central charge
PASS C3 for h1 != 0 the central branch is a trivial direct sum: after H' = H + (h2/h1) D the FULL structure tensor equals that of h2 = 0 (algebra x R)
PASS C3b control: for h1 = 0 (Galilei) NO shift H' = H + tD removes the h2 term (the difference [K,P] = h2 D survives for all t): the mass extension is non-trivial
